        "noSubjects": "No obstacles yet.",
        "gmNotes": "<p><strong>Example: Chase, Competitive.</strong> Both sides race for the same goal. Built for four level-2 PCs: base DC 16, easy 14. Six obstacles.</p><p>At the midsummer festival, teams carry a lit lantern across the town to the bell tower. The party races the Harrow brothers. Rounds are about a minute.</p><p><strong>Each round:</strong> both teams roll initiative to set who goes first. The Harrows move at a steady pace: 1 obstacle each round on Next round.</p><p><strong>Each roll:</strong> a success earns 1 Chase Point, a critical success 2, and a critical failure loses 1. Use + and − on the obstacle. When it is full, mark it Complete, add 1 to Party and reveal the next obstacle. Chase Points don't carry over.</p><p><strong>The Lantern</strong> is a counter: if a critical failure would drop the lantern, lower it by 1. At 0 it goes out, and the team must relight it at the start, losing a round.</p><p><strong>It ends</strong> when a team gets past obstacle 6 and rings the bell. A tie goes to the side that acted first that round.</p>",
